      en: "A prominent urban clock tower in Diriamba, built in the early 20th century as a symbol of the economic boom brought by coffee. Clock Tower of Diriamba is known for: inaugurated in 1935 during the heyday of the coffee industry, the clock mechanism was brought from germany, it reaches a height of 15.5 meters. This region plays an important role in Nicaragua's geography and culture and represents a significant part of the national heritage."
