      en: "A majestic white basilica in the central square of Diriamba, playing a key role in the city's colorful festivals. San Sebastián Basilica (Diriamba) is known for: construction work began in 1891 and was completed in 1939, it is the center of the famous 'el güegüense' dance performances, achieved the status of a minor basilica in 1964. This region plays an important role in Nicaragua's geography and culture and represents a significant part of the national heritage."
