      en: "A historic stone church at the end of the main street in Granada, not far from the shores of the vast Lake Nicaragua. Guadalupe Church (Granada) is known for: originally founded by monks in the year 1626, used as a fortress by william walker's troops in the 19th century, after severe destruction, it was rebuilt in all its glory. This region plays an important role in Nicaragua's geography and culture and represents a significant part of the national heritage."
